{
  "name": "The Pequod",
  "provenance": "Drawn from the format by an agentling of this project, 2026-08-07, from the ops vocabulary in packages/shared/src/scene.ts and nothing else. No third-party art, image, atlas or palette is included or derived from: every op here is hand-placed and every colour is either a DB32 entry (packages/shared/src/palette.ts, DawnBringer's 32-colour palette, 2012, freely usable) or one of three near-black values mixed for this pack. The setting is the between-decks of a nineteenth-century whaler at night, a scene of the kind Melville's Moby-Dick (1851, public domain) describes; the name \"The Pequod\" and the whaling furniture — gunports, oil lamps, harpoon irons, oil casks — are from that public-domain text and from the common historical record, not from any film, game or studio adaptation, whose designs and marks are deliberately not reproduced. Ours to commit, ours to change, no attribution owed to anyone outside this repository.",
